From: Loong <1031313955@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] defenvs: nokia_xg-040g-mf: reach the recovery page, and flash from it

The mirror of 951 for xg-040g-mf.  Two halves, same as there.

Getting in.  Both paths that used to end in TFTP now end in httpd: holding
reset at power-on, and a failed boot.  check_buttons is also spliced into
the front of _firstboot -- on a first migration the environment is not built
yet, so without it the button is never looked at on the one boot where the
user is most likely to be holding it.

Flashing.  Two httpd_* scripts next to the board's own ubi_write_*: writing
BL2 goes through mtd with an offset so mtd itself skips the first 0x800
bytes (BootROM looks for the FIP there), and formatting UBI is ubi_format
minus the trailing reset, so the same session can go on to write volumes.
httpd.c prefers these env scripts and falls back to a built-in equivalent
when they are missing -- when a board needs rescuing, the env on flash is
exactly the copy most likely to be stale or broken.

httpd_write_fip is carried over from 954 rather than left to the built-in
fallback: a routine bootloader update must not evict rootfs_data, and having
the script present makes that explicit in the board's own environment.

TFTP is untouched -- the bootmenu entries and every boot_tftp* variable stay
where they are.  Automatic paths go to the browser, manual ones keep TFTP.

Not carried over from the md side: 952's bootmenu branding (menu entry 9 to
start the server by hand, the About entry, envver-driven refresh) and 953's
back-to-stock.  The branding needs an equivalent of the EVT_POST_PREBOOT hook
that currently lives in board/airoha/an7581/, and back-to-stock is measured
from the md model's factory flash and cannot be reused here at all.  So on
this board the recovery page is reached by holding reset or by a failed boot,
not from the menu.

--- a/defenvs/an7583_nokia_xg-040g-mf_env
+++ b/defenvs/an7583_nokia_xg-040g-mf_env
@@ -26,7 +26,8 @@ boot_production=led $bootled_status on ; run ubi_read_
 boot_first=if button reset ; then led $bootled_status on ; run boot_default ; fi ; bootmenu
 boot_default=run bootcmd ; run boot_tftp_forever
 boot_production=led $bootled_status on ; run ubi_read_production && bootm $loadaddr#$bootconf ; led $bootled_status off
-boot_ubi=run boot_production ; run boot_tftp_forever
+boot_ubi=run boot_production ; run boot_httpd_forever
+boot_httpd_forever=while true ; do httpd ; sleep 1 ; done
 boot_tftp_forever=led $bootled_status on ; while true ; do run boot_tftp ; sleep 1 ; done
 boot_tftp_production=tftpboot $loadaddr $bootfile_upg && env exists replacevol && iminfo $loadaddr && run ubi_write_production ; if env exists noboot ; then else bootm $loadaddr#$bootconf ; fi
 boot_tftp_recovery=tftpboot $loadaddr $bootfile && env exists replacevol && iminfo $loadaddr && run ubi_write_recovery ; if env exists noboot ; then else bootm $loadaddr#$bootconf ; fi
@@ -34,7 +35,10 @@ preboot=led $bootled_status on
 boot_tftp_write_bl2=mw.b $loadaddr 0xff 0x800 ; setexpr loadaddr_bl2 $loadaddr + 0x800 ; tftpboot $loadaddr_bl2 $bootfile_bl2 && run mtd_write_bl2
 boot_tftp_write_fip=tftpboot $loadaddr $bootfile_fip && run ubi_write_fip && run reset_factory
 preboot=led $bootled_status on
-check_buttons=if button reset ; then run boot_tftp ; fi
+check_buttons=if button reset ; then httpd ; fi
+httpd_write_bl2=mtd erase bl2 && mtd write bl2 $loadaddr 0x800 $filesize
+httpd_format_ubi=ubi detach ; mtd erase ubi && ubi part ubi
+httpd_write_fip=if ubi check fip ; then ubi write $loadaddr fip $filesize ; else run ubi_write_fip ; fi
 ethaddr_factory=ubi read 0x90000000 ri && env readmem -b ethaddr 0x9000003e 0x6 ; setenv ethaddr_factory
 part_default=production
 reset_factory=ubi part ubi ; mw $loadaddr 0x0 0x800 ; ubi write $loadaddr ubootenv 0x800 ; ubi write $loadaddr ubootenv2 0x800
@@ -48,6 +52,6 @@ _init_env=setenv _init_env ; run ubi_create_env ; save
 ubi_write_fip=run ubi_remove_rootfs ; ubi check fip && ubi remove fip ; ubi create fip 0x100000 static && ubi write $loadaddr fip $filesize
 ubi_write_production=ubi check fit && ubi remove fit ; run ubi_remove_rootfs ; ubi create fit $filesize dynamic && ubi write $loadaddr fit $filesize
 _init_env=setenv _init_env ; run ubi_create_env ; saveenv ; saveenv ; run ubi_create_board_data
-_firstboot=setenv _firstboot ; run ethaddr_factory ; run _switch_to_menu ; run _init_env ; run boot_first
+_firstboot=setenv _firstboot ; run check_buttons ; run ethaddr_factory ; run _switch_to_menu ; run _init_env ; run boot_first
 _switch_to_menu=setenv _switch_to_menu ; setenv bootdelay 3 ; setenv bootmenu_delay 3 ; setenv bootmenu_0 $bootmenu_0d ; setenv bootmenu_0d ; run _bootmenu_update_title
 _bootmenu_update_title=setenv _bootmenu_update_title ; setenv bootmenu_title "$bootmenu_title       [33m$ver[0m"
